        "steps": [
          {
            "description": "In a medium pot, bring a few inches of water to a boil over medium heat then salt the water.",
            "image": ""
          },
          {
            "description": "Trim the broccoli rabe and cut it into 1 1/2 to 2 inch lengths. Simmer in boiling water to reduce bitterness, about 4 to 5 minutes. Then cold shock in ice water and drain very well. ",
            "image": ""
          },
          {
            "description": "Heat a Dutch over or large soup pot over medium high heat with extra virgin olive oil, a turn of the pan. Add the sausage and brown and crumble, 7 to 8 minutes. Add the onions and garlic and cook for a few more minutes. Add the thyme and lemon zest, then add broccoli rabe and season with a little nutmeg. Stir in the stock and bring to a boil. Simmer a few minutes to combine flavors. Turn off heat, cool and store for a make ahead meal. ",
            "image": ""
          },
          {
            "description": "Reheat stoup over low heat and bring to a low boil. Add the pasta and cook to al dente, about 10 minutes. ",
            "image": ""
          },
          {
            "description": "Ladle the stoup in shallow bowls and garnish with cheese. Serve with crusty bread for mopping.",
            "image": ""
          }
